{"id":7167,"date":"2022-08-05T18:46:37","date_gmt":"2022-08-05T18:46:37","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/?post_type=student&#038;p=7167"},"modified":"2024-10-31T10:06:40","modified_gmt":"2024-10-31T10:06:40","slug":"hanifatu-napari-mumuni","status":"publish","type":"student","link":"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/student\/hanifatu-napari-mumuni\/","title":{"rendered":"Hanifatu Napari Mumuni"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<div class=\"wp-block-cover profile-banner bg-alt\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-cover__background has-background-dim-100 has-background-dim\" style=\"background-color:none\"><\/span><div class=\"wp-block-cover__inner-container\">\n\n\n<a href=\"javascript:history.back()\"> <div class=\"profiles-btn\"> \n\n<div class=\"btn-left-sq bg-primary\"> <i class=\"fa fa-caret-left white-text\"> <\/i> <\/div>\n<div class=\"btn-text title-bold white-text\">Back to Profiles<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n<\/a>\n\n<h2 class=\"profile-name\">Hanifatu Napari Mumuni<\/h2>\n\n<p class=\"primary-bold profile-position prof-pos\"><span class=\"primary-text is-bold\"><\/span>Ghana<\/p>\n\n<p class=\"profile-info profile-tagline primary-bold prof-pos\"><span class=\"primary-text is-bold\"><\/span>Lecturer &#8211; Tamale Technical University<\/p><\/div><\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"is-layout-flow wp-block-group pad-5 profile-body\"><div class=\"wp-block-group__inner-container\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/4\/2022\/08\/Hanifatu-Napari-Mumuni.jpg\"\/>\n\n<p class=\"profile-testimonial invis\"><span class=\"primary-text is-bold\"><\/span> <\/p>\n\n<p class=\"profile-success invis\"><span class=\"primary-text is-bold\"><\/span> <\/p>\n\n<p class=\"profile-studentbio invis\"><span class=\"primary-text is-bold\"><\/span> <\/p>\n\n\n<p>Hanifatu Napari Mumuni is an Lecturer and the Head of the Statistics Department at the Tamale Technical University (TATU). She is also a PhD holder in Applied Statistics from the University for Development Studies, where her research was tailored toward software reliability growth models. At the Department of Statistics of TATU, she serves as a mentor to students providing them with career guidance and other professional support aside from providing them with course content that has meaningful application in real-life. AIMS-Ghana has been a major part of her success story, equipping her with programming and public speaking skills as an academic and researcher. Skills in Latex and programming languages like Python have metamorphosed her PhD journey into a beautiful one. As a Mastercard Foundation Scholar, AIMS Ghana ignited her passion for giveback to society leading to the organisation and facilitation of hands-on coding for beginners in her community and online participants.<\/p>\n<\/div><\/div>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Hanifatu Napari Mumuni is an Lecturer and the Head of the Statistics Department at the Tamale Technical University (TATU). She is also a PhD holder in Applied Statistics from the University for Development Studies, where her research was tailored toward software reliability growth models. At the Department of Statistics of TATU, she serves as a<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":12,"featured_media":7168,"parent":0,"template":"","meta":{"advgb_blocks_editor_width":"","advgb_blocks_columns_visual_guide":"","profile-testimonial":"","profile-success":"","profile-studentbio":"","profile-studentname":"Hanifatu Napari Mumuni","profile-country":"Ghana","profile-program":"Lecturer - Tamale Technical University"},"tags":[],"student_types":[13],"acf":[],"featured_img":"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/4\/2022\/08\/Hanifatu-Napari-Mumuni.jpg","coauthors":[],"author_meta":{"author_link":"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/author\/joel\/","display_name":"joel"},"relative_dates":{"created":"Posted 3 years ago","modified":"Updated 1 year ago"},"absolute_dates":{"created":"Posted on August 5, 2022","modified":"Updated on Oct